From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lite3-zig <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:08:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report hash-probe exhaustion distinctly

When all LITE3_HASH_PROBE_MAX probe slots for a key hold other keys,
lookups and inserts both returned EINVAL, indistinguishable from invalid
arguments. A lookup now returns ENOENT (the key cannot be present), and
an insert returns ENOSPC (no slot left), so applications can recognise
- and rate-limit - inputs crafted to collide under the unseeded DJB2
hash.
---
 src/lite3.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lite3.c b/src/lite3.c
index a623c2e..4ed062e 100644
--- a/src/lite3.c
+++ b/src/lite3.c
@@ -327,8 +327,9 @@ int lite3_get_impl(
 			}
 		}
 	}
-	LITE3_PRINT_ERROR("LITE3_HASH_PROBE_MAX LIMIT REACHED\n");
-	errno = EINVAL;
+	// Every probe slot held a different key, so this key is not present.
+	LITE3_PRINT_ERROR("KEY NOT FOUND (LITE3_HASH_PROBE_MAX SLOTS PROBED)\n");
+	errno = ENOENT;
 	return -1;
 }
 
@@ -819,8 +820,11 @@ insert_append:
 		LITE3_PRINT_DEBUG("OK\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
+	// Every probe slot holds a different key: no slot left for this one.
+	// Distinct from EINVAL so callers can tell (possibly adversarial) hash
+	// collisions from invalid arguments.
 	LITE3_PRINT_ERROR("LITE3_HASH_PROBE_MAX LIMIT REACHED\n");
-	errno = EINVAL;
+	errno = ENOSPC;
 	return -1;
 }
 
